/**
@mainpage reSIProcate API Documentation

reSIProcate is a set of C++ libraries and applications for building SIP
endpoints, proxies and media servers.  Source code, issues and the wiki are at
https://github.com/resiprocate/resiprocate.

@section main_libraries Libraries

- @ref rutil_main "rutil": utility classes used by everything else, including
  resip::Data, logging and the DNS resolver.
- @ref resip_main "resip": the RFC 3261 SIP stack (resip::SipStack).  It parses
  and builds SIP messages and handles transactions, transports and RFC 3263 DNS
  lookups.
- @ref dum_main "dum": the Dialog Usage Manager (resip::DialogUsageManager), a
  higher-level API above the stack for building SIP user agents and servers
  (no media).
- @ref recon_main "recon": a SIP user agent library with media support above
  dum (recon::ConversationManager, recon::UserAgent).
- @ref reflow_main "reflow": media flows for recon, with STUN, TURN, SRTP and
  DTLS-SRTP (flowmanager::FlowManager).
- @ref media_main "resipmedia": SDP and RTP port helpers shared by recon's
  media stacks.
- @ref return_main "reTurn client": a STUN/TURN client library
  (reTurn::TurnAsyncSocket).

@section main_applications Applications

- @ref repro_main "repro": a SIP proxy, registrar and presence server
  (repro::Proxy, repro::ReproRunner).
- @ref return_main "reTurn server": a STUN/TURN server.

@section main_grouped Grouped Classes

The SIP stack tags its most important classes with these groups:
- @ref resip_crit
- @ref sip_grammar
- @ref sip_parse
- @ref make_sip
- @ref resip_config
*/
